    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n990" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγύ̆ρ-της</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγείρω</span>)
		prop. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>collector</i>, esp.
				<i>begging priest</i> of Cybele, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μητρὸς ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.218
				</span></i>
			 (Al.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γάλλοις ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					141.1
				</span></i>
			:— then, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>vagabond</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				503
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				715
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lysipp.
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Clearch.
				5
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόλιος ἀ.</span>, of Tiresias,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				388
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ μάντεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					364b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a throw of the
			dice, <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				57.5
			</span></i>. (On the accent cf. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.77
			</span></i>.)</div>
